Defect: SMI-INVALID-DATE https://pysnmp.github.io/pysmi/stable/mib-defects.html#smi-invalid-date

The module's only REVISION clause carries an empty string for its date.
By convention the newest REVISION carries the LAST-UPDATED date, and
this is the only one, so the repair gives it the LAST-UPDATED value,
201603161455Z. That is inferred from the convention, not read from the
vendor.

No publisher on record serves this module, so the baseline is the text
this repository carried before the repair; which publication that was is
not recovered.

--- a/SLE-VRRP-MIB
+++ b/SLE-VRRP-MIB
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
 				" "
 			DESCRIPTION 
 				"This MIB contains information about RIP version 2."
-			REVISION ""		-- 
+			REVISION "201603161455Z"		-- 
 			DESCRIPTION 
 				"OSFPv2"
 			::= { sleMgmt 57 }
